  "reason": "Managed harness chat lifecycle fixes (HARN-1..6, 13, 14) in harnesses.py, mcp.py, mcp_gateway.py, automation_runtime.py and one api.py naming call. Tool-event ToolCall lookups and every unpaged oldest-first list_entities scan in harnesses.py now filter in SQL (find_entities by status/run_id/session_id/profile) or are bounded/offset-paged, so the tool ledger, restart recovery, run/session lookups and session_activity keep working past the first 1,000-row page. A turn cancelled or shut down while still connecting now settles INTERRUPTED (stream_turn, shutdown, startup) instead of reserving the chat forever. The MCP gateway server contains a per-request CancelledError so a late approval decision no longer closes its single-use socket; any terminal turn path retires the turn's pending approvals and interactions and resolves their waiters with a denial. Stop and the turn's end cancel in-flight gateway work tracked per turn, foreground command timeouts are clamped below the vendor tool timeout, and a cancelled foreground command terminates its process. Session rollovers close the superseded vendor session once idle. The subagent/messaging binding derives from the conversation's durable settings, not transient request flags. Grok developer instructions travel once per connection, conversation naming runs a gateway-free analysis session, and a steer that races completion returns a coherent not-active state. The selection covers the harness runtime, adapters, transports, MCP gateway, provider subagents, approvals, agent messaging, automation runtime (foreground command cancellation) the row-horizon AST guard now that harnesses.py is enforced by it, and test_harness_activity_cost.py because this branch was rebased onto #567, which changed the same activity, follower and session_activity paths. Each new regression test seeds the pre-1,000-row or race condition and fails on origin/main 51c543c; the selection passes 431/431 locally on 18c0d71.",
  "exclusions": "Full suites are not approved and are excluded. missions.py stays exempt in the row-horizon guard (owned by claude/mission-recovery). No frontend, native or Playwright tests: this is a backend-only change with no ui/ or Rust edits and no new visible controls, so playwright is []. test_harnesses.py, test_harness_provider_subagents.py and test_automation_runtime.py are selected by node, excluding nine nodes that fail identically on pristine origin/main (verified on 51c543c) and are outside HARN-1..6/13/14: test_harnesses.py::test_workspace_retrieval_reports_actionable_argument_errors (3 params; expects a 'Required: <field>' message, main returns the raw validator text), ::test_harness_gateway_lists_scoped_sources_with_url_metadata and ::test_browser_gateway_rechecks_conversation_binding_before_execution (expect a raised HarnessConfigurationError, main now returns a normalized failure result); test_harness_provider_subagents.py::test_operator_limit_reaches_the_harness_and_is_enforced (expects limit wording absent from the normalized refusal), ::test_harness_answers_a_subagent_question_with_subagent_message and ::test_harness_gets_unread_subagent_messages_at_its_next_turn (subagent question/message delivery, P3/P4 scope); test_automation_runtime.py::test_host_scope_expiry_closes_running_commands (a background command's session is still closing after its 0.8 s wait; it does not reach the foreground-cancel path this change adds). All other nodes in those files and every other listed file run in full.",
